{"title":"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Coordinate_Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Coordinate Geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Only_Pythagorean_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Only Pythagorean Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Similarity)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Similarity)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Pythagorean_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Pythagorean Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/ccc55f85ae3c39ddd90ace7764a57bce879351c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=8$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a4826138756e48059393331c30916b2b06430cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=6$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10eaae211abee4558967d69b313e979a506ccce2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{ME}\\perp\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />. What is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b97d5e6d663a54035d16ce34566969c20b57636.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AME$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfd669122ec38473832e3e4c235b333911960055.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } \\frac{65}{8} \\qquad \\text{(B) } \\frac{25}{3} \\qquad \\text{(C) } 9 \\qquad \\text{(D) } \\frac{75}{8} \\qquad \\text{(E) } \\frac{85}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"381\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Coordinate_Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Coordinate_Geometry)\">Solution 1 (Coordinate Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Coordinate Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of the diagonal, it would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/563948106c3332662355412547d99acab218c16f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. The diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> would be the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a18a289fc98f530f1fec87c43f99201693ec8e76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{3x}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a30c9c946a561bfb130894432aa55948d58b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, its line would be in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/1/2e16c211b130e6f7b963c13f352f3b94d7c64db1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -\\frac{4x}{3} + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"38\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> would give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/955e5e0ddd2115b2314441e9779473a2ce628203.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{25}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"52\" height=\"37\" />. To find the x-intercept of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/2/f32ad1fd669956a52fb9c45b4008cd21a883d1da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -\\frac{4x}{3} + \\frac{25}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"38\" /> we plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/7/797aea66a2e6d0c2bd0e42934604820432b904ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{25}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"38\" />. Then, using the Shoelace Formula for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> , <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/563948106c3332662355412547d99acab218c16f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/d/28df05cbc19f58ab2f52f6e000564e90854800cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{25}{4}, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"38\" />, we find the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/8/3e80cb0974edb419706cbf0df69447440bf49038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{75}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b10f5f4c5b8bf3a582dbca5a38107354e8327fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.75cm); defaultpen(0.8); pair A=(0,0), B=(8,0), C=(8,6), D=(0,6), M=(A+C)/2; path ortho = shift(M)*rotate(-90)*(A--C); pair Ep = intersectionpoint(ortho, A--B); draw( A--B--C--D--cycle ); draw( A--C ); draw( M--Ep ); filldraw( A--M--Ep--cycle, lightgray, black ); draw( rightanglemark(A,M,Ep) ); draw( C--Ep ); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,Ep,S); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,NW); [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"258\" />\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">Pythagorean theorem</a> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb8ffc595afa0b86b2545d16f07c48faa8dd004.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c67c8e84a7b8145439aa10391babf5ced6c623f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM=5$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>The triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/4957ac13f1da771a229ae10cab117d16eafda806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AME$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> have the same angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and a right angle, thus all their angles are equal, and therefore these two triangles are similar.\n</p><p>The ratio of their sides is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0df872da9ac832a94513fbb4a51a2e60e965faa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AM}{AB} = \\frac 58$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" />, hence the ratio of their areas is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/d/b2dc1e2381f2005128f7c83e6e5dd3ee3aedf53d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( \\frac 58 \\right)^2 = \\frac{25}{64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"91\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p>And as the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/55441fe7f2e54e9e8d5bc4ce503780f33e356ea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6\\cdot 8}2 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"77\" height=\"37\" />, the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/4957ac13f1da771a229ae10cab117d16eafda806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AME$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/2/9d25f9b383fe41734d282ad44c9794402c58472e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24\\cdot \\frac{25}{64} = \\boxed{ \\frac{75}8 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"111\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Only_Pythagorean_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Only_Pythagorean_Theorem)\">Solution 3 (Only Pythagorean Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Only Pythagorean Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b10f5f4c5b8bf3a582dbca5a38107354e8327fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.75cm); defaultpen(0.8); pair A=(0,0), B=(8,0), C=(8,6), D=(0,6), M=(A+C)/2; path ortho = shift(M)*rotate(-90)*(A--C); pair Ep = intersectionpoint(ortho, A--B); draw( A--B--C--D--cycle ); draw( A--C ); draw( M--Ep ); filldraw( A--M--Ep--cycle, lightgray, black ); draw( rightanglemark(A,M,Ep) ); draw( C--Ep ); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,Ep,S); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,NW); [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"258\" />\n</p><p>Draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a771251838750a4cb9926c5e2b03324b2b2edae7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> as shown from the diagram. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> is of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, because of the midpoint <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. Through the Pythagorean theorem, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/e/3de8578650711f71b87553a5570981df9a09c500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE^2 = AM^2 + ME^2 \\implies 25 + ME^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"294\" height=\"16\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/6/7e63b5c24aa577735ed135ea3f199e93d2099650.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = \\sqrt{25 + ME^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" />. Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a30c9c946a561bfb130894432aa55948d58b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> for the sake of clarity. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3ed29175c1a94a73ba86b3aeb7e724355e72e25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB = 8 - \\sqrt{25 + x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"160\" height=\"21\" />. From here, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/8/6484a7437c0b340349751ed0e0448e2f4d340954.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE^2 = CB^2 + BE^2 = ME^2 + MC^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"283\" height=\"16\" />. From here, we can write the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/b/23b6a1418ee663f468871490cbedb61640a41be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2 + (8 - \\sqrt{25 + x^2})^2 = 5^2 + x^2 \\implies 36 + (64 - 16\\sqrt{25 + x^2} + 25 + x^2) = 25 + x^2 \\implies 100 - 16\\sqrt{25 + x^2} \\implies \\sqrt{25 + x^2} = \\frac{25}{4} \\implies 25 + x^2 = \\frac{625}{16} \\implies 400 + 16x^2 = 625 \\implies 16x^2 = 225 \\implies x = \\frac{15}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"1049\" height=\"76\" />. Now, remember <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/0/e50c9f0906ff3d8bfcca7bc207acac29f58f3da6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE \\neq \\frac{15}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af27e7b6513b857fefcc176f217553ad839db1f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{15}{4} = ME$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"38\" />, since we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/b/04b6f83ebaddf5f05b73516e28350493792ddee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = ME$\" width=\"68\" height=\"12\" /> in the start of the solution. Now to find the area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bf6c21e0a84438e3b1658c1bb764501506c68e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{4} \\cdot 5 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{75}{8} = CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"169\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Similarity.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Similarity)\">Solution 4 (Similarity)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Similarity)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9739c4b47d01217f2b0dbe404e972ccc6199725b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM = \\frac{10}{2} = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"115\" height=\"38\" /> by the Pythagorean theorem, and furthermore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b97d5e6d663a54035d16ce34566969c20b57636.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AME$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> is similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35b8d98205768ab343f59cb3a4f116529835c684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME = 5 \\cdot \\frac{6}{8} = \\frac{15}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"142\" height=\"38\" />, and the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e460fc3dc8921fbf0cd7d1d60c87339cbea98bd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot \\frac{15}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = \\boxed{\\frac{75}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"130\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Pythagorean_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Pythagorean_Theorem)\">Solution 5 (Pythagorean Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Pythagorean Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b10f5f4c5b8bf3a582dbca5a38107354e8327fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.75cm); defaultpen(0.8); pair A=(0,0), B=(8,0), C=(8,6), D=(0,6), M=(A+C)/2; path ortho = shift(M)*rotate(-90)*(A--C); pair Ep = intersectionpoint(ortho, A--B); draw( A--B--C--D--cycle ); draw( A--C ); draw( M--Ep ); filldraw( A--M--Ep--cycle, lightgray, black ); draw( rightanglemark(A,M,Ep) ); draw( C--Ep ); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,Ep,S); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,NW); [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"258\" />\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, we claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72ef59078f894d92215e582cc9f8b3e0d79fb76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />. It then follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/e/21e34403824ae50b8d1bd899e42da86c5b8c77da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM \\cong MC = 5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"15\" /> \n</p><p>Because we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711d16a8898a1716ca32a20ee1b36855e178bb44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM \\cong MC, \\angle AME \\cong \\angle CME,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"251\" height=\"18\" /> and reflexive side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/f/4afc0b14ca58c4f35514e7cfa7adb0bd55226f2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/3/983748a1de72e27e6f8b8d54c52e5c1a2543f1bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AME \\cong \\triangle CME.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" /> By CPCTC, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5c84bf9c5c026233c36e61cb45ae7f2e415737.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE \\cong EC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" /> For the sake of simplicity, we'll call those side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/457c659da9158194f44f23d493ebaca415a53177.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0de0d7775f45eebbf82014af63cd67c8a309e269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE = 8 - x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" /> We can now set up the Pythagorean theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cf85f676e9d4b408d7f74ecd19f491159276355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EBC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add05f408b994336bc36777be58113a4935f553e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(8 - x)^2 + 6^2 = x^2.\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"20\" /> Combining like terms and simplifying gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1a3b303b8199da9da6c83111811f330cca8a99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-16x + 100 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"15\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a7eee80f3e31af514db3be2f25019ee7a434b76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{25}{4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>It helps to think that in order to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/5/2c575b3e6bbd320af00a72f21551cb995488054a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[AME],$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" /> we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6a5dab0650ea78f80ca12d62afe83905de42ceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MC}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8a4553ac233956f79bfaf678fc53a42aed12681.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{EM}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/f/04faa14876e5f0c45c01394dace1d47124832239.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EM = y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> Applying the Pythagorean Theorem to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b9957aef1820459e452f991248a28374a6655e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CME$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/7/5c7106738f0b23e74f3ec5bd9594143cae4005af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^2 + y^2 = \\left(\\frac{25}{4} \\right)^2.\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"46\" /> Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> (this is not that difficult) gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11e5a8e7384cc3cb3727f797b63dda128a2d0ea0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{15}{4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" /> So, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b97d5e6d663a54035d16ce34566969c20b57636.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AME$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/4/f448e08184686541d9ad39c9a62b888907264923.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{15}{4} \\cdot 5}{2} = \\frac{75}{8} \\implies \\boxed{D}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"173\" height=\"42\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72ef59078f894d92215e582cc9f8b3e0d79fb76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea7633e0071ed1b50736e672804123c279d8fe59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" />. Drop the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> call it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91ad89046e9d6b2654aa563659330182c256f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN = 3$\" width=\"69\" height=\"12\" />, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the centre of the rectangle. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/e/3ee868fba5915382c910db34cc6ce2620cb24f99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NA = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />. Now, consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/c/7ec59623df538c6d642402d0f5400adbda30afa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EMN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />. Quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5f921891e1163cb02551b1eba7c4fc7c9e7ea2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EBCM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic and thus if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/15157918db35645ecb347ab13158eadba3e4e7e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MEA = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe65644aedb6d29ff61c17fac1b47d0f68754d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MEB = 180-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"16\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03e5d297eef4072ff2b103f7eb5d7c5debb95151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />, The two triangles are similar, and because both are 3-4-5 right triangles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab207cea213cc093d1072f7d2cbfb955858a5a62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x = 3 \\implies x = \\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"152\" height=\"38\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/c/f0c73d4bfe558ba925ad0d190399b2e485705460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NE = 3 \\cdot \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{9}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" />. Thus the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/4957ac13f1da771a229ae10cab117d16eafda806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AME$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cdc6f41f6c869c9b8abc88fef0d773293b533e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + \\frac{9}{4} = \\frac{25}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" /> and the height is 3, and thus the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8d4d42c977151f5f3b12c17c769c7b536167393.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{25}{4} \\cdot 3 = \\boxed{\\frac{75}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"130\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B\">2009 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 AMC 1